{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SzeChunYiu/ORION/pulls/1469","id":4371162299,"node_id":"PR_kwDOT5fCLM8AAAABBIqkuw","html_url":"https://github.com/SzeChunYiu/ORION/pull/1469","diff_url":"https://github.com/SzeChunYiu/ORION/pull/1469.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/SzeChunYiu/ORION/pull/1469.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SzeChunYiu/ORION/issues/1469","number":1469,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"[R12][AB] Prove production registries are not identifiable from optimizer outputs","user":{"login":"SzeChunYiu","id":52784502,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNzg0NTAy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52784502?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SzeChunYiu","html_url":"https://github.com/SzeChunYiu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SzeChunYiu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SzeChunYiu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SzeChunYiu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SzeChunYiu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SzeChunYiu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SzeChunYiu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SzeChunYiu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SzeChunYiu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SzeChunYiu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Clean child of the executed R6M rejection stack at exact parent `533a8e15dc20fd875eb442b573fd72eb9264b218`.\n\nThe completed 31,457,280-evaluation gate independently confirmed every declared R6M optimizer value but rejected production transfer because no complete production move registry was declared. R12 proves that this rejection is mathematically necessary rather than a paperwork gap.\n\n## Exact theorem increment\n\nFor a finite state space, semantics map and support measure, distinguish:\n\n- direct optimum over the feasible semantic class;\n- a semantics-preserving, resource-decreasing production move registry;\n- maximum resource of a registry-terminal state.\n\nR12 proves:\n\n1. for every `n>=2`, the same feasible states, semantics, resources, optimum value and optimum witness admit one complete declared registry with terminal complexity `n` and another with terminal complexity `1`;\n2. therefore optimizer I/O and optimum witnesses cannot identify production terminal complexity or registry completeness;\n3. a single unresolved legal edge can change terminal complexity while agreeing with every resolved trace/membership observation;\n4. observed execution traces certify only a lower inventory of existing moves, not absence of unobserved moves;\n5. completeness requires either an extensional legal-move enumeration or a schema theorem covering every implementation operation and parameter instance.\n\nThe ambiguity gap is unbounded.\n\n## Source-bound R6M diagnosis\n\nAt exact source commit `1e18787841d99d76a3c7661505838d2eca8780db`, the workflow binds:\n\n- protocol blob `48214ac16ce956a109cbce39a25d59b77eb95b3a`;\n- runner blob `ead51fc9d03e25acf3d65557cb0f08fd1eb98873`.\n\nThe bound source is a direct optimizer: local option tables, a 512-state XOR DP, exact backtracking, Restore accounting and witness verification. It does not expose a production successor relation, rewrite registry or legal-move predicate. That source can prove the frozen minimum without defining production terminality.\n\nThis does not claim that no larger external compiler has rewrites. Such a compiler must supply its actual operation interface and completeness argument.\n\n## Exact finite result\n\nWorkflow run `33019636182` is GREEN and now requires byte-exact equality between two fresh regenerations and the committed result.\n\n- predecessor source-bound run/job: `33019293566` / `98345369363`;\n- registries: `33,866`;\n- size-six registries: `32,768`;\n- direct optimizer signature: identical for every registry;\n- terminal complexities: every value from one through `n` at each `n=2,...,6`;\n- empty/chain ambiguity through `n=32`: gap `31`;\n- result SHA-256: `d4f14be666dceb2da71bfac01a25fd32c6fd7bc947734db1d0f945bc10487cf0`;\n- source-bound artifact SHA-256: `705c5dfffc799b61056bbfb295382b2049f9936bed1028bda0410b80ee8100b4`.\n\nTerminal:\n\n`AB_REGISTRY_NONIDENTIFIABILITY_R12_PASS`\n\n## Scientific disposition\n\nThe earlier execution terminal remains authoritative:\n\n`FINITE_PRODUCTION_REALIZATION_CERTIFICATE_REJECTED__PRODUCTION_REGISTRY_NOT_DECLARED_COMPLETE`.\n\nIt cannot be repaired by relabeling optimizer candidates or traces as moves. A future transfer must bind either a complete extensional move predicate/enumeration or a complete external operation grammar with schema/parameter coverage and an omitted-schema hostile control.\n\nThe abstract XOR/finite-group and interaction-tax theorems remain valid in their declared complete fusion languages. R6M production terminal complexity, compiler performance and physical resource value remain not established.\n\n## Authority boundary\n\nGeneric rewriting, transition systems, conformance testing and black-box identification are donor-owned. The residual AB contribution is the exact certificate-ownership boundary: optimizer correctness, proof-language terminality and production-registry completeness are distinct authorities and cannot promote one another.\n\nNo production transfer, compiler speedup, physical-resource claim, novelty certificate, external review or journal authority follows.\n\nPart of #1385 and #1421.","created_at":"2026-08-26T22:20:38Z","updated_at":"2026-08-26T22:30:28Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"779158f886d4b59e05c80c9aa0ac45c7f873a164","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":true,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SzeChunYiu/ORION/pulls/1469/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.